; i1 division and remainder: undefined behavior, poison, and the few defined
; cases.
;
; - x / 0 and x % 0 are UB, as is a poison divisor.
; - sdiv 1, 1 and srem 1, 1 are INT_MIN / -1 (-1 / -1 = 1 does not fit): UB.
;   So the only defined signed division is 0 / 1 (0 / -1 = 0).
; - a poison dividend gives poison for udiv / urem, but for sdiv / srem with
;   divisor 1 (= -1) it is UB, since the dividend may be INT_MIN.
; - `exact` never bites at i1: the only defined quotients have remainder 0.
; - a vector division is UB if any lane is.
;
; Each UB instruction carries a `<- UB` marker comment, and `ASSERT UB <line>`
; names its line (filled in by tests/ub/fill-ub-lines.py).
;
; Generated by tests/llvm-arith/i1/gen-i1.py -- edit the generator, not this file.

